Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: apple: add T6050 with WFI in both states

T6050 (M5 Pro/Max) had no cpuidle driver, so suspend-to-idle never
reached cpuidle_enter_s2idle(): the tick was never frozen and
timekeeping never suspended. Register the driver on apple,t6050.

CPU PD writes CYC_OVRD, which is locked on T6050, so the power-down
entry is replaced by a copy of the WFI entry (cpu_do_idle(), which
saves the lost registers since patch 0012). Index 1 is kept because
the generic s2idle selector skips fallback index 0, and it is not
marked CPUIDLE_FLAG_OFF, which would hide it from s2idle too. Older
chips keep their existing states.

Ported from aurora-silicon/linux (integration/aurora), GPL-2.0-only OR MIT:
  4253ee01142c Erik Bourget: cpuidle: apple: Add T6050
  e82e308db725 Bartosz Nitka: keep a selectable WFI state at index 1
  a391e5394aad Jonathan Goyvaerts: do not mark that state CPUIDLE_FLAG_OFF
The T8140/T6041/T8132 cases and the OF match table are not ported.

---
diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
index 3d2b804df..72c2ca477 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
@@ -124,6 +124,17 @@ static struct cpuidle_driver apple_idle_driver = {
 
 static int apple_cpuidle_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
+	/*
+	 * CPU PD writes CYC_OVRD, which is locked on T6050 (the write
+	 * faults). Its WFI already lets the hardware power-gate idle cores,
+	 * and cpu_do_idle() saves the state that WFI loses there, so both
+	 * entries must use WFI. Keep index 1: the generic s2idle selector
+	 * skips fallback index 0, otherwise tick_freeze() and timekeeping
+	 * suspension are never reached.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t6050"))
+		apple_idle_driver.states[STATE_PWRDOWN] = apple_idle_driver.states[STATE_WFI];
+
 	return cpuidle_register(&apple_idle_driver, NULL);
 }
 
@@ -158,7 +169,8 @@ static int __init apple_cpuidle_init(void)
 	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t6030") ||
 	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t6031") ||
 	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t6032") ||
-	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t6034")))
+	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t6034") ||
+	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t6050")))
 		return 0;
 
 	pdev = platform_device_register_simple("cpuidle-apple", -1, NULL, 0);
